            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Term | Meaning (Plain English) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Ion** | An atom (or group of atoms) that has acquired an electric charge by losing or gaining electrons | $\\text{Na}^+$, $\\text{Cl}^-$ |\n| **Cation** | A positively charged ion formed when an atom **loses** electrons | $\\text{Na}^+$, $\\text{Mg}^{2+}$ |\n| **Anion** | A negatively charged ion formed when an atom **gains** electrons | $\\text{Cl}^-$, $\\text{O}^{2-}$ |\n| **Ionic (electrovalent) bond** | The strong electrostatic attraction between oppositely charged ions formed by the transfer of electrons from a metal to a non-metal | The bond holding $\\text{Na}^+$ and $\\text{Cl}^-$ in $\\text{NaCl}$ |\n| **Ionic compound** | A chemical compound held together by ionic bonds | $\\text{NaCl}$, $\\text{MgO}$, $\\text{MgCl}_2$ |\n| **Crystal lattice** | A regular, repeating three-dimensional framework of alternating positive and negative ions | The crystal structure of table salt |\n| **Formula unit** | The simplest whole-number ratio of ions represented in an ionic compound (not a discrete molecule) | $\\text{NaCl}$, $\\text{MgCl}_2$, $\\text{Al}_2\\text{O}_3$ |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Ion** | Aisa atom jisne electron diye ya liye ho, to uspar charge aa gaya | Na⁺, Cl⁻ |\n| **Cation** | Positive ion: atom ne electron **diye** | Na⁺, Mg²⁺ |\n| **Anion** | Negative ion: atom ne electron **liye** | Cl⁻, O²⁻ |\n| **Ionic (electrovalent) bond** | Ek metal ne electron diye, ek non-metal ne liye, aur ulte charge wale ions ke beech ka **aakarshan** | Na⁺ aur Cl⁻ ke beech |\n| **Ionic compound** | Ionic bond se bana compound | NaCl, MgO |\n| **Crystal lattice** | Ions ka regular, baar-baar dohrane wala 3D jaal | NaCl ka crystal |\n| **Formula unit** | Ionic compound ke formula wala sabse chhota ginti ka group (molecule nahi) | NaCl, MgCl₂ |"
