            "body": "In the previous topic, we learned that **oxidation** means gaining oxygen (or losing hydrogen), **reduction** means losing oxygen (or gaining hydrogen), and both always happen together. Even the browning of a sliced apple was a small everyday oxidation reaction. Today we see how this same chemistry shapes our daily lives: burning fuel on a stove, iron rusting in damp air, oils and snacks turning stale, and our own cells breathing to keep us alive. At the end, we will bring the entire chapter together in a single summary.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Pichhle topic mein humne seekha ki **oxidation** matlab oxygen ka judna (ya hydrogen ka nikalna), **reduction** matlab oxygen ka nikalna (ya hydrogen ka judna), aur dono hamesha saath hote hain. Kate seb ka bhoora hona bhi isi ka ek chhota example tha. Aaj hum dekhenge ki yehi chemistry hamare aas-paas har roz kaise chal rahi hai: gas ka chulha jalna, loha zang khana, tel-ghee ka baasi ho jaana, aur hamare apne sharir mein saans ka kaam. Aakhir mein poore chapter ka saar."
