            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "In the previous chapter, we saw how hydrogen sits at the top-left corner of the periodic table while oxygen sits in Group 16, and how every element's position reveals its chemical personality. Now let's bring those two elements together and examine the most famous compound they form: **water**—something we drink every single day without ever pausing to ask, \"What actually is this stuff?\"",
            "bodyHinglish": "Pichhle chapter mein humne dekha ki periodic table mein hydrogen sabse upar-left kone mein aur oxygen Group 16 mein baitha hai, aur har tatva ki position uska swabhav batati hai. Ab in dono ko jodkar dekhte hain ki unse bana sabse mashhoor compound kaisa hai: **paani**, jise hum roz peete hain par shayad kabhi \"kya hai ye?\" nahi poocha."
