            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Up to this point, you have visualised gases through a **particle model**: particles spaced far apart, zipping about randomly at high speeds, and constantly colliding with container walls. In this chapter, we take a major leap forward: learning how to **measure** a gas and asking what happens when we tweak one property while keeping others under control. In this opening topic, we will not jump straight into complex equations. First, we must master the **four fundamental measurements** of any gas (pressure, volume, temperature, and amount) alongside their **units and conversions**—because in chemistry, an incorrect unit ruins the entire calculation. We will wrap up with a preview of Boyle's Law.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab tak tumne gaason ko dekha hai ek **particle picture** ke roop mein: kan door-door, random, tez, aur deewaron se takrate hue. Is chapter mein hum ek kadam aage jaate hain: gas ko **naapna** aur ye poochna ki jab hum ek cheez badalte hain to baaki kya badalta hai. Aur is pehle topic mein koi niyam nahi sikhenge. Pehle sirf **chaar naap** (pressure, volume, temperature, matra) aur unki **ikaaiyan** (units) seekhenge, kyunki unit galat to saara hisaab galat. Aakhir mein agle topic ke Boyle ke niyam ki jhalak milegi."
