            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Across the previous topics, we dissected the four fundamental variables of a gas ($P, V, T, n$), formulated the three classical gas laws, and explored molar volume at STP. Now comes the most important skill in practical chemistry: **recognising which law governs any given real-world situation**. In this culminating topic, we begin with a bus winding down a mountain road, explore ear-popping, lung mechanics, scuba diving physiology, and weather balloons, establish a comprehensive decision flowchart, tackle over ten mixed numerical problems, reinforce vital safety protocols, and conclude with an executive chapter summary.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Pichhle topics mein humne gaason ke chaar variables (P, V, T, matra) aur teen niyam seekhe, phir STP, Avogadro ka niyam aur molar volume. Ab sabse zaroori kaam: **kaun sa niyam kab lagana hai** ye pehchanna. Is topic mein ek ghat road ki bus yatra se shuru karke ear popping, tyre, saans lena, balloon, gotakhor ke bubbles aur scuba tank jaise **10 se zyada mixed problems** hal karenge, ek decision flow banayenge, safety yaad karenge, aur aakhir mein poore chapter ka saar dekhenge."
