            "body": "| Term | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Hydrogen** | The lightest element, symbol H, atomic number 1; a non-metal gas | Makes up the vast majority of the Sun |\n| **Diatomic molecule** | A molecule made of two atoms | H₂, O₂, Cl₂ |\n| **Valency** | The number of bonds an atom can form (concept from Chapter 5) | The valency of hydrogen is 1 |\n| **Protium** | The most common isotope of hydrogen: 1 proton, 0 neutrons | ¹₁H, about 99.98 percent |\n| **Deuterium** | An isotope of hydrogen: 1 proton, 1 neutron | ²₁H |\n| **Tritium** | The radioactive isotope of hydrogen: 1 proton, 2 neutrons | ³₁H, extremely rare |\n| **Heavy water** | Water in which ordinary hydrogen is replaced by deuterium | D₂O |\n| **Hydrocarbon** | A compound of hydrogen and carbon (studied in detail in higher classes) | Gasoline, LPG, candle wax |",
