            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Over the past five topics, we have explored hydrogen from every angle: what its atom and isotopes look like, how it is prepared in the school lab, how it is manufactured in industry, what physical and chemical properties it has, and where its uses and hazards lie. Now comes the most rewarding part: **putting all those pieces together**. Starting with a rainy-day riddle game in the school science club, we will work through **14 solved problems** covering \"which method?\", \"which metal?\", \"who am I?\", balanced equations, balloon lift, fuel energy, and connections across Chapters 5 to 10—followed by a master summary of the entire chapter.",
