            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "In our previous chapter, we observed that burning hydrogen produces only water vapour, making it an exceptionally clean fuel. But what do we mean when we describe something as \"clean\"? Cleanliness is measured against a fundamental benchmark: **clean air**. As the final chapter of Class 9 Chemistry, this study directly concerns the very air we breathe every second of our lives. In this topic, we begin by examining the exact composition of pristine air (expressed in percentages and parts per million), explore the layered structure of Earth's atmosphere, and investigate what constitutes **air pollution**, where pollutants originate, and how the **Air Quality Index (AQI)** quantifies air quality. This topic sets the foundation for our upcoming explorations of acid rain, the greenhouse effect, the ozone layer, urban smog, and practical technological remedies.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Pichhle chapter mein humne dekha ki hydrogen jalne par sirf paani banata hai, yaani wo ek saaf eendhan ban sakta hai. Ab sawaal ye hai: **saaf** ka matlab hum kis se compare karke kehte hain? Jawab hai **saaf hawa**. Ye Class 9 Chemistry ka aakhri chapter hai, aur ye hamari **saans** se juda hai. Is topic mein hum pehle dekhenge ki saaf hawa mein kya-kya hota hai (percent aur ppm mein), atmosphere ki parton (layers) ko jaanenge, phir samjhenge ki **pradushan (pollution)** kya hota hai, kahan se aata hai, aur use naapne ka **AQI** kaise padhte hain. Ye chapter ka **parichay** hai; acid rain, greenhouse effect, ozone, smog aur samadhan agle topics mein aayenge."
