            "heading": "Key Vocabulary",
            "headingHinglish": "Naye shabd",
            "body": "| Term | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Atmosphere** | The thick blanket of gases surrounding planet Earth | All atmospheric layers taken together |\n| **ppm (parts per million)** | A unit expressing very small concentrations: the number of parts of a substance per million ($10^6$) parts of the mixture | 420 ppm $\\text{CO}_2$ |\n| **Troposphere** | The lowest layer of the atmosphere (extending to about 12 km), where all weather events occur | Clouds, rainfall, and the air layer below passenger flights |\n| **Stratosphere** | The layer directly above the troposphere (extending from roughly 12 km to 50 km); hosts the protective ozone layer | Stratospheric ozone shield |\n| **Pollutant** | Any undesirable substance introduced into the air in a location or concentration that causes harm to living organisms or the environment | $\\text{CO}$, $\\text{SO}_2$, soot |\n| **Primary pollutant** | A pollutant emitted directly from an identifiable source into the atmosphere | Carbon monoxide ($\\text{CO}$) from automobile exhaust |\n| **Secondary pollutant** | A pollutant formed in the atmosphere when primary pollutants undergo chemical reactions with one another or with natural air components | Ground-level ozone, atmospheric acid rain droplets |\n| **Particulate matter (PM)** | Microscopic airborne solid particles or liquid droplets suspended in the atmosphere | Dust, fly ash, soot |\n| **PM10 and PM2.5** | Particulate matter with diameters up to 10 micrometres and 2.5 micrometres, respectively | Inhalable coarse dust and fine combustion particles |\n| **AQI (Air Quality Index)** | A standardized numerical scale (typically 0 to 500) used by environmental agencies to communicate daily air quality to the public | The electronic advisory board at the school gate |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Shabd | Matlab (simple bhasha mein) | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Atmosphere (vaayumandal)** | Earth ke charon taraf gas ki moti parat | Hawa ki saari parte milkar |\n| **ppm (parts per million)** | 10 lakh hisson mein kitne hisse: bahut chhoti matra batane ka tareeka | 420 ppm CO₂ |\n| **Troposphere** | Sabse neeche ki parat (lagbhag 12 km tak), jahan mausam banta hai | Baadal, baarish, hawai jahaaz ke neeche ki parat |\n| **Stratosphere** | Troposphere ke upar ki parat (lagbhag 50 km tak); ozone layer isi mein hai | Ozone layer |\n| **Pollutant (pradooshak)** | Hawa mein galat jagah ya galat matra mein aayi wo cheez jo nuksaan karti hai | CO, SO₂, soot |\n| **Primary pollutant** | Jo seedhe kisi source se nikalta hai | Gaadi ke dhuen ki CO |\n| **Secondary pollutant** | Jo hawa mein doosri cheezon ke milne se banta hai | Zameen ke paas ka ozone |\n| **Particulate matter (PM)** | Hawa mein tairte bahut chhote thos ya boond ke kan | Dhool, soot |\n| **PM10 aur PM2.5** | Wo kan jinki chaudai 10 ya 2.5 micrometre tak hai | Dhool aur dhuen ke kan |\n| **AQI (Air Quality Index)** | Hawa kitni saaf ya gandi hai, ye batane wala ek number (0 se 500) | Gate ka board |"
