            "heading": "Chapter Summary: Atmospheric Pollution in Review",
            "headingHinglish": "Chapter Ka Saar: Atmospheric Pollution",
            "body": "| Topic | Core Scientific Themes | Summary Takeaway |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Topic 1** | Clean Air Composition, Pollutants, and the AQI | Clean dry air consists of ~78% $\\text{N}_2$, 21% $\\text{O}_2$, 0.93% $\\text{Ar}$, and ~0.04% $\\text{CO}_2$. Pollutants are classified as primary or secondary. The Air Quality Index (0–500) quantifies health risk. Fine PM2.5 particles are ~28 times thinner than a human hair. |\n| **Topic 2** | Acid Rain | Industrial $\\text{SO}_2$ and vehicular $\\text{NO}_x$ oxidize into sulfuric ($\\text{H}_2\\text{SO}_4$) and nitric ($\\text{HNO}_3$) acids, lowering rain pH below 5.6 and corroding marble monuments ($\\text{CaCO}_3 + \\text{H}_2\\text{SO}_4 \\rightarrow \\text{CaSO}_4 + \\text{H}_2\\text{O} + \\text{CO}_2$), while acidifying aquatic ecosystems. |\n| **Topic 3** | Greenhouse Effect and Global Warming | Natural greenhouse gases ($\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$, $\\text{CO}_2$, $\\text{CH}_4$) trap terrestrial infrared radiation, keeping Earth habitable (+15°C instead of -18°C). Anthropogenic emissions have surged $\\text{CO}_2$ to ~420 ppm, driving an enhanced greenhouse effect and sea-level rise. Burning 1 L of petrol generates ~2.28 kg of $\\text{CO}_2$. |\n| **Topic 4** | The Ozone Layer and Its Depletion | Stratospheric ozone ($\\text{O}_3$, 15–35 km) filters lethal solar UV-B radiation. Synthetic CFCs release chlorine radicals that catalytically destroy ~100,000 ozone molecules each. The universal 1987 Montreal Protocol successfully phased out CFCs, enabling ongoing planetary shield recovery. |\n| **Topic 5** | Smog, Particulate Matter, and Health | Winter temperature inversions trap pollutants beneath a warm \"thermal ceiling\", creating sulfurous smog. Photochemical smog generates ground-level ozone. PM2.5 penetrates deep into lung alveoli. Carbon monoxide binds blood haemoglobin with 200× the affinity of oxygen. N95 respirators block $\\ge 95\\%$ of fine particles. |\n| **Topic 6** | Clean Air Technologies and Retrospective | Catalytic converters ($\\text{Pt/Pd/Rh}$), flue-gas limestone scrubbers, electrostatic precipitators (ESPs), ultra-low-sulfur fuels ($\\le 10\\text{ ppm}$), renewable electricity, and green hydrogen work alongside individual conservation to restore clean skies. |",
            "bodyHinglish": "| Topic | Kya seekha | Ek line |\n|---|---|---|\n| Topic 1 | Hawa aur pradushan: parichay aur AQI | Hawa lagbhag 78% N₂, 21% O₂ aur baaki ke saath banti hai; galat matra ya jagah par hanikarak cheez pollutant hai; AQI se hawa ki quality padhte hain; PM10 aur PM2.5 bahut chhote kan hain. |\n| Topic 2 | Acid rain | SO₂ aur nitrogen oxides baarish ke paani mein ghulkar acid banate hain, jo marble, jheel, mitti aur dhaatu ko nuksan pahunchate hain (CaCO₃ + H₂SO₄ → CaSO₄ + H₂O + CO₂). |\n| Topic 3 | Greenhouse effect aur global warming | CO₂ jaisi gaasein dharti ki garmi rokti hain; prakritik effect zaroori hai par insaan ne use badha diya hai (1 L petrol lagbhag 2.3 kg CO₂). |\n| Topic 4 | Ozone layer aur uska kam hona | Stratosphere ki ozone UV rokti hai; CFC mein se nikla chlorine atom ozone todta hai; Montreal Protocol se layer dheere theek ho rahi hai. |\n| Topic 5 | Smog, particulate matter aur sehat | Dhuan aur kohra milkar smog banta hai; PM2.5 phephdon mein gehre jaata hai; CO khoon mein oxygen ki jagah le leti hai; bure AQI par bachaav zaroori. |\n| Topic 6 | Saaf hawa ke upay | Catalytic converter, scrubber, ESP, BS-VI, CNG, renewable energy, green hydrogen, ped aur roz ki aadatein; pollution diary se apna asar badalna. |"
